      "locked": false,
      "text": "-> Reduce latency from seconds into milliseconds\n-> Reduce read call to DB. (IO calls)\n\nIssue\n-> if cache goes down all call goes to DB. (some time it is acceptable for few hours or min)\n-> record invalidation (steal data).\n-> cache referesh.\n\nLet's see what we achieved\n1) Handle 10M request/second (low latency and high thourghput)\n2) Avalability\n3) Scalabilty\n4) Eventual Consistency (remember both consistency and partition tolerance won't achieved)\n\nWe discuss each point separately because it becomes lengthy.\n1) Server (stateless and stateful)\n2) Cache (eviction, cache write)\n3) DB (selection)\n4) Load balancer (Algorithm, Type of LB (L4 and L7))\n5) Messaging component (Rabbit MQ, Kafka)\n6) Searching Component (Elastic Search)\n7) Calls/connections (Rest API, websocket,gRpc)\n8) In Memory (Redis)\n9) Propagate Events (Fan in, Fan Out, SSE, Redis-pusub,kafka)\n10) Blob Storage (S3)\n11) We try to cover Capacity Estimation as well (Tricky part)\n\nAs I understand above points used to create below System\n1) Whatsapp\n2) Youtube\n3) TicketMaster\n4) Google drive\n5) News feed\n6) Uber (Tracking required geo location DB (Postgress, Redis)\n7) Zomato or Swiggy \n8) Search Autocomplete ( tree structure or document based search)\n9) Search Engine\n\n\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "-> Reduce latency from seconds into milliseconds\n-> Reduce read call to DB. (IO calls)\n\nIssue\n-> if cache goes down all call goes to DB. (some time it is acceptable for few hours or min)\n-> record invalidation (steal data).\n-> cache referesh.\n\nLet's see what we achieved\n1) Handle 10M request/second (low latency and high thourghput)\n2) Avalability\n3) Scalabilty\n4) Eventual Consistency (remember both consistency and partition tolerance won't achieved)\n\nWe discuss each point separately because it becomes lengthy.\n1) Server (stateless and stateful)\n2) Cache (eviction, cache write)\n3) DB (selection)\n4) Load balancer (Algorithm, Type of LB (L4 and L7))\n5) Messaging component (Rabbit MQ, Kafka)\n6) Searching Component (Elastic Search)\n7) Calls/connections (Rest API, websocket,gRpc)\n8) In Memory (Redis)\n9) Propagate Events (Fan in, Fan Out, SSE, Redis-pusub,kafka)\n10) Blob Storage (S3)\n11) We try to cover Capacity Estimation as well (Tricky part)\n\nAs I understand above points used to create below System\n1) Whatsapp\n2) Youtube\n3) TicketMaster\n4) Google drive\n5) News feed\n6) Uber (Tracking required geo location DB (Postgress, Redis)\n7) Zomato or Swiggy \n8) Search Autocomplete ( tree structure or document based search)\n9) Search Engine\n\n\n",
